SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
Subject: [PATCH] printk: guard Lumia 920 panic-console reactivation
Upstream-Source: https://github.com/UEFI-code/linux-6.6-lumia920
Upstream-Revision: 9872e9316212490b7db8e3371fa1d63bd3394cc5
License-Provenance: existing GPL-2.0-only SPDX header in kernel/panic.c

A complete debug-off link exposed an unconditional panic-path caller outside
of the initially focused objects. Gate its declarations and reactivation with
the same option; retain the original panic behavior when explicitly enabled.
No normal panic logic or physical hardware values are changed.

--- a/kernel/panic.c
+++ b/kernel/panic.c
@@ -265,8 +265,10 @@
 		crash_smp_send_stop();
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_LUMIA920_EARLY_DEBUG
 extern u8 lumiafb_enabled;
 void lumiafb_early_init(void);
+#endif
 
 /**
  *	panic - halt the system
@@ -278,8 +280,10 @@
  */
 void panic(const char *fmt, ...)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_LUMIA920_EARLY_DEBUG
 	if (!lumiafb_enabled)
 		lumiafb_early_init();
+#endif
 	
 	static char buf[1024];
 	va_list args;
